From f6aed791240e2df775f447f101a8fc36cc9626cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fieldmar <974888+fieldmar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:33:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] camellia: ship the gold connectivity firmware

Pin the BT, MCU and Wi-Fi connsys firmware to the matched set from
Redmi/vnd_gold/gold:12/TP1A.220624.014/V14.0.1.0.TNQCNXM, the set crDroid
14 shipped (crdroidandroid/android_device_xiaomi_camellia 8b32ce3802).
This reverts e3a5ded for the _1_1 variants and moves the _1a_1 variants
to gold as well, so the whole set stays matched.

With the stock V14.0.6.0 firmware (BT build 20230710), some earbuds
(Soundcore A3i) never answer AVDTP SUSPEND, so A2DP drops about 15 s
after a pause. Working around that with INTEROP_DISABLE_AVDTP_SUSPEND
keeps A2DP started during eSCO, and the AP btcvsd path then delivers
silence on every BT-mic session after the first (WhatsApp calls, voice
recorders). With the gold set (BT build 20230224) every SUSPEND is
accepted within ~0.25 s, music survives pause, and repeated BT-mic
sessions work without the quirk.

BT, MCU and Wi-Fi files must stay a matched set: mixing the gold BT
image with stock MCU/Wi-Fi breaks connsys RF calibration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
